# Evidence signing key — EXAMPLE FILE. Contains no secret; safe to commit.
#
# The evidence bundle seal (Phase 1) needs key material. The code reads
# EITHER of these, in this precedence order:
#
#   1. ROUTE_ONE_EVIDENCE_KEY         -- inline value (dev only)
#   2. ROUTE_ONE_EVIDENCE_KEY_FILE    -- path to a key file (recommended)
#
# NOTE: putting these in .env does NOT work. There is no python-dotenv in this
# repo, and evidence_integrity.load_key() calls os.getenv() directly. pydantic
# reads .env for AppConfig fields, but the signing key is not one of them.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# METHOD A — inline (quick, dies with the shell)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# In the SAME terminal that starts the backend:
#
#   export ROUTE_ONE_EVIDENCE_KEY=$(openssl rand -hex 32)
#   echo ${#ROUTE_ONE_EVIDENCE_KEY}      # expect 64
#   python -m app.main                   # backend must start in THIS shell
#
# A new terminal = no key = sealed:false bundles.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# METHOD B — key file (recommended; survives shell restarts)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   mkdir -p /kaggle/working/R1v0.1/backend/keys
#   openssl rand -hex 32 > /kaggle/working/R1v0.1/backend/keys/evidence.key
#   chmod 600 /kaggle/working/R1v0.1/backend/keys/evidence.key
#   export ROUTE_ONE_EVIDENCE_KEY_FILE=/kaggle/working/R1v0.1/backend/keys/evidence.key
#
# ABSOLUTE paths, deliberately. This file previously said $PWD/backend/keys/,
# which is correct from the repo root and broken from backend/ -- and from
# Kaggle's default cwd of /kaggle/working, which is neither. A relative path
# fails as a bare shell redirect error with no hint that the path is the
# problem, so the key silently goes unreadable.
#   python -m app.main
#
# backend/keys/ and *.key are gitignored. Keep it that way.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRITICAL — DO NOT ROTATE CASUALLY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The key is baked into every sealed manifest's signature. Change or lose it
# and EVERY previously sealed bundle fails verification — you lose the ability
# to prove anything you already produced. Generate once per engagement, store
# it, and back it up somewhere the client controls.
#
# For the LASTMA/State deployment the annex commits to a State-held KMS key
# and Route One not holding it. That is the METHOD B shape with the file
# owned by the State, and the Signer interface swapped for an asymmetric
# implementation (Ed25519) — HMAC is symmetric and gives no non-repudiation.
